WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.737 --> 00:00:05.572
ALBERT LIN (VOICEOVER):
Quinsachata Volcano

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:08.308
last erupted only a
few thousand years ago.

00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:20.587
AMELIA PEREZ TRUJILLO: This
is pumice, volcanic rock.

00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:22.155
ALBERT LIN (VOICEOVER):
I head for the summit

00:00:22.222 --> 00:00:24.858
with Peruvian archaeologist
Amelia Perez Trujillo.

00:00:28.495 --> 00:00:29.896
We follow the flow of lava.

00:00:32.766 --> 00:00:35.235
We're meeting my
LiDAR team at the top.

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:43.309
I'm looking for
evidence that this

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:47.180
was a sacred site for people
who were here before the Inca.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:51.551
MAN: You guys ready to fly?

00:00:51.618 --> 00:00:52.886
ALBERT LIN: Just about, yep.

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:54.120
MAN: OK.

00:00:54.187 --> 00:00:54.921
Props up.

00:01:09.636 --> 00:01:11.271
ALBERT LIN: These
are all troopers.

00:01:11.337 --> 00:01:13.973
Right here, just
over that edge there.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.074
Look at that.

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:20.947
WOMAN: [speaking spanish]

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:22.449
ALBERT LIN (VOICEOVER):
These suggest

00:01:22.515 --> 00:01:25.385
that people were
burying their ancestors

00:01:25.452 --> 00:01:29.222
close to a god-like event.

00:01:29.289 --> 00:01:31.191
WOMAN: [speaking spanish]

00:01:49.042 --> 00:01:50.710
ALBERT LIN: You can imagine
that when it erupted,

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:55.014
it must have sent wonder, awe,
just disbelief into the minds

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:56.349
of the people all around it.

00:01:56.416 --> 00:01:58.518
WOMAN: [speaking spanish]

00:01:58.585 --> 00:01:59.752
ALBERT LIN: All
the material went

00:01:59.819 --> 00:02:01.688
that way, towards the city.

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:04.624
WOMAN: [speaking spanish]

00:02:04.691 --> 00:02:06.559
ALBERT LIN: Incredible.

00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:10.730
ALBERT LIN (VOICEOVER): The
lava stretches for over a mile.

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:13.466
At its base is a small
town called Raqch'i.

00:02:21.975 --> 00:02:24.878
These must be the manmade
structures that I could

00:02:24.944 --> 00:02:28.781
see on the satellite imagery.

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:36.789
WOMAN: [speaking spanish]

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:38.458
ALBERT LIN: This whole
area, all of these

00:02:38.525 --> 00:02:41.127
were homes of people that
existed hundreds of years

00:02:41.194 --> 00:02:42.362
before the Inca.

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:43.863
WOMAN: [speaking spanish]

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:46.533
ALBERT LIN: And they built
their homes next to a volcano.

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:48.635
Amazing.

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:51.304
(VOICEOVER) pre-Inca pilgrims
weren't the only ones

00:02:51.371 --> 00:02:52.438
to have left their mark here.

00:02:55.808 --> 00:02:59.245
Wow, it's incredible.

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:01.314
WOMAN: [speaking spanish]

00:03:17.997 --> 00:03:18.898
ALBERT LIN: Amazing.

00:03:18.965 --> 00:03:19.999
What was it for?

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:23.269
WOMAN: [speaking spanish]

00:03:23.336 --> 00:03:25.538
ALBERT LIN: The
temple of Wiracocha.

00:03:25.605 --> 00:03:30.076
I have a document that I found
from the Spanish Chronicles

00:03:30.143 --> 00:03:31.611
WOMAN: [speaking spanish]

00:03:31.678 --> 00:03:35.415
ALBERT LIN: It says when the
Inca ruler passed by this area,

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:38.585
he saw the shrine of Wiracocha.

00:03:38.651 --> 00:03:43.957
The people told him the miracle
of fire that fell from the sky.

00:03:44.023 --> 00:03:46.259
He decided that the
remembrance should be greater

00:03:46.326 --> 00:03:49.495
and ordered the erection
of a large building.

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:52.632
This was done, and there
was no larger building

00:03:52.699 --> 00:03:53.866
in the land of the Inca.

00:03:56.402 --> 00:03:58.705
Kind of sends
shivers up your spine

00:03:58.771 --> 00:04:03.610
when you read something that
was written, you know, in 1557,

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:07.747
and you're standing here looking
at it still standing today.

00:04:07.814 --> 00:04:09.248
WOMAN: [speaking spanish]

00:04:21.394 --> 00:04:23.830
ALBERT LIN (VOICEOVER): There
seems to be a pattern emerging.

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:27.567
The Inca incorporate aspects
of earlier belief systems

00:04:27.634 --> 00:04:32.805
and make them theirs by
building bigger and better.

00:04:32.872 --> 00:04:37.477
This is architecture of power,
just like at Machu Picchu.

